      "content": "Experimentally reducing a functional group cannot be done by which one of the following reagents?",
      "options": [
        {
          "identifier": "A",
          "content": "Pt-C/H<sub>2</sub>"
        },
        {
          "identifier": "B",
          "content": "Na/H<sub>2</sub>"
        },
        {
          "identifier": "C",
          "content": "Pd-C/H<sub>2</sub>"
        },
        {
          "identifier": "D",
          "content": "Zn/H<sub>2</sub>O"
        }
      ],
      "correct_options": [
        "B"
      ],
      "explanation": "Na in presence of H<sub>2</sub>, will not release electron\nwhich are required for reduction.\n<br><br>H<sub>2</sub> gas also not get adsorbed on Na. Hence\nNa/H<sub>2</sub> cannot be used as a reducing agent."
